  "$comment": "Query vocabulary for `tecton search`: what an agent is likely to type (key) and the words the guideline files use for the same thing (value). A key is one word, or a phrase that fires only when the query has its words in that order (`pin code`, not `pin` alone, so \"pin a column\" stays with Table). Keys and values go through the search tokenizer (lowercased, stemmed); agent:build fails when a key loses a word to the stopwords, when two keys stem to the same words, when a value is not a single word some entry uses, or when a key only expands to itself. Built into agent/index.json by `pnpm --filter @tecton/react agent:build`.",
